##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "In how many ways can 5 different candies be distributed among 4 children? (Children could get 0 candies or more than one candy) Choices: A)4^5 B)5^4 C)5! D)4! E)4!*5!", "step": "There are in total 5 candies. Let's say A,B,C,D and E.\nCandy A can be distributed among any 4 children. So, there are 4 ways of distributing candy A.\nsimilarly candy B,C,D and E can be distributed in 4 ways.\nSo total ways of distribution is\n4*4*4*4*4 = 4^5.\nANS:A", "answer": "A"}, "Answer": "A", "Step": "For one particular arrangement of men, say {m1, m2, m3} women in the front row can be arranged in 3!=6 ways, as total # of arrangements of men is 3!=6 then total # of arrangements of men and women is 3!*3!=36.\nANS:D", "Response": ["A"], "Attempt answer": "A", "Solved": true, "Total solved": 21, "Total executed": 42, "Accuracy": 0.5}
##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A is 30% more efficient than B. How much time will they, working together, take to complete a job which A along could have done in 23 days? Choices: A)11 days B)13 days C)20 3\u204417 days D)12 days E)None of these", "step": "Ratio of times taken by A and B = 100 : 130 = 10 : 13.\nSuppose B takes x days to do the work.\nThen, 10 : 13 : : 23 : x \u21d2 x = (23\u00d713)/10 \u21d2 x = 299\u204410\nA\u2019s 1 day\u2019s work = 1\u204423; B\u2019s 1 days work = 10\u2044299\n(A + B)\u2019s 1 day\u2019s work = (1\u204423 + 10\u2044299) = 23\u2044299 = 1\u204413\n\u2234 A and B together can complete the job in 13 days.\nAnswer B", "answer": "B"}, "Answer": "B", "Step": "For one particular arrangement of men, say {m1, m2, m3} women in the front row can be arranged in 3!=6 ways, as total # of arrangements of men is 3!=6 then total # of arrangements of men and women is 3!*3!=36.\nANS:D", "Response": ["C"], "Attempt answer": "C", "Solved": false, "Total solved": 21, "Total executed": 43, "Accuracy": 0.4883720930232558}
