##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A man says that he gained 10 percent as profit in selling a suitable cloth material. He says if he had purchased the same one 10 percent cheaper than it was actual and if he had sold it for 20% profit he gets 25paise less. find at what price he sold the suit? Choices: A)10.5 B)11.2 C)12.5 D)13.5 E)15.8", "step": "Let cp = 100 then sp = 110;\nwhen cp= 90 then sp = 108;\nNow when 200p less sp = 108\nSo 25 p less, sp = 108/200*25=13.5\nANSWER:D", "answer": "D"}, "Answer": "D", "Step": "Let the salaries of A and B be 9x and 4x.\n9x \u00d7 115\u2044100 = 5175\n\\ x = 500\n\\ salary of B = 500 \u00d7 4 = 2000\nAnswer A", "Response": ["D"], "Attempt answer": "D", "Solved": true, "Total solved": 39, "Total executed": 69, "Accuracy": 0.5652173913043478}
##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "Tanya's grandfather was 8 times older to her 16 years ago. He would be 3 times of her age 8 years from now. What was ratio of ages of Tanya and her grandfather 8 years ago. Choices: A)11:50 B)11:51 C)11:53 D)11:54 E)None of these", "step": "Let, Tanya age 16 years ago = x,\nGrandfather's age 16 years ago = 8x.\n8 years from now, 3(x+16+8) = (8x+16+8)\n=> x = 48/5\n8 years ago ratio was:\n=>x+8/8x+8=48/5+8/8\u00d748/5+8\n=>88/424=11/53\nOption C", "answer": "C"}, "Answer": "C", "Step": "Let the salaries of A and B be 9x and 4x.\n9x \u00d7 115\u2044100 = 5175\n\\ x = 500\n\\ salary of B = 500 \u00d7 4 = 2000\nAnswer A", "Response": ["N"], "Attempt answer": "N", "Solved": false, "Total solved": 39, "Total executed": 70, "Accuracy": 0.5571428571428572}
