##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A batsman has scored an average of 46 runs for a certain number of innings played in England. When he came back to India, he played another two test matches of two innings each and scored at an average of 55 runs. For the innings in England and in India taken together, he has improved his average by 2 runs over the matches played in England. Find the number of innings played in England. Choices: A)12 B)13 C)14 D)15 E)16", "step": "Let the number of innings played in England be x.\n\u2234 Total runs scored in England = 46x\nTotal runs scored for innings played in India\n= 55 \u00d7 4 = 220\n(\u2235 the number of innings played in India = 4)\nAlso, 46x+220/x+4 = 48\n\u21d2 46x + 220 = 48 x + 192\n\u21d2 2x = 28\n\u21d2 x = 14\nAnswer C", "answer": "C"}, "Answer": "C", "Step": "A team of 6 members has to be selected from the 10 players. This can be done in 10C v 6 or 210 ways.\nNow, the captain can be selected from these 6 players in 6 ways.\nTherefore, total ways the selection can be made is 210\u00d76= 1260\nANSWER:D", "Response": ["B"], "Attempt answer": "B", "Solved": false, "Total solved": 48, "Total executed": 91, "Accuracy": 0.5274725274725275}
