##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A rectangle has twice the area of a square. The length of the rectangle is 14 cm greater than that side of the square whereas breadth is equal to side of the square. Find the perimeter of the square? Choices: A)34 B)38 C)56 D)28 E)19", "step": "Let side of square be x.\nThen for rectangle length = 14 + x and breadth = x.\nIt is given\nArea of rectangle = 2 \u00d7 (area of square)\nlength \u00d7 breadth = 2(x \u00d7 x)\n(x + 14) \u00d7 x = 2 \u00d7 x2\nx2 + 14x = 2x2\nx2 = 14x\nx = 14.\nPerimeter of square = 4 \u00d7 x = 56\nAnswer: C", "answer": "C"}, "Answer": "C", "Step": "A team of 6 members has to be selected from the 10 players. This can be done in 10C v 6 or 210 ways.\nNow, the captain can be selected from these 6 players in 6 ways.\nTherefore, total ways the selection can be made is 210\u00d76= 1260\nANSWER:D", "Response": ["C"], "Attempt answer": "C", "Solved": true, "Total solved": 51, "Total executed": 95, "Accuracy": 0.5368421052631579}
