##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A, B and C start at the same time in the same direction to run around a circular stadium. A completes a round in 252 seconds, B in 308 seconds and c in 198 seconds, all starting at the same point. After what time will they again at the starting point ? Choices: A)26 minutes and 18 seconds B)42 minutes and 36 seconds C)45 minutes D)46 minutes and 12 seconds E)46 minutes", "step": "L.C.M. of 252, 308 and 198 = 2772.\nSo, A, B and C will again meet at the starting point in 2772 sec. i.e., 46 min. 12 sec.\nAnswer: Option D", "answer": "D"}, "Answer": "D", "Step": "Patients not seen = 35 - 21 = 14\nPatients not seen percentage = (14/35 x 100) %\n= 40%\nAnswer : A", "Response": ["L"], "Attempt answer": "L", "Solved": false, "Total solved": 101, "Total executed": 190, "Accuracy": 0.531578947368421}
##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A house sold for $500,000 in 1990 and sold ten years later for $400,000. By what percent did the value of the house change? Choices: A)20% B)0% C)-10% D)-20% E)-25%", "step": "% Change= (F-I)/I x100, where F is the final value and I is the initial value.\n($400,000-$500,000)/$500,000= -0.2. A negative value means that the house fell in value. Thus, the value of the house dropped by 20%\nAnswer D", "answer": "D"}, "Answer": "D", "Step": "Patients not seen = 35 - 21 = 14\nPatients not seen percentage = (14/35 x 100) %\n= 40%\nAnswer : A", "Response": ["A"], "Attempt answer": "A", "Solved": false, "Total solved": 101, "Total executed": 191, "Accuracy": 0.5287958115183246}
##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "The distance between Omaha and Lincoln is 60 miles. John drives a car that gets 30 miles per gallon of gas, and David drives a car that gets 20 miles per gallon. How many more gallons of gas does David use on a round trip from Omaha to Lincoln? Choices: A)2 B)3 C)4 D)5 E)6", "step": "Ratio of John Car efficiency : David Car efficiency = 30:20\nRound trip takes 120 miles. Hence converting any one of the base for 120 = 180:120\nMeans if David travel 120 miles for the same gallons Omaha travled 180 miles. The gallon required to travel extra 60 miles is\nHence = 60/30 = 2\nAnswer : A", "answer": "A"}, "Answer": "A", "Step": "Patients not seen = 35 - 21 = 14\nPatients not seen percentage = (14/35 x 100) %\n= 40%\nAnswer : A", "Response": ["A"], "Attempt answer": "A", "Solved": true, "Total solved": 102, "Total executed": 192, "Accuracy": 0.53125}
