##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "A train running at a speed of 100 miles/hour, takes 10 hours to reach its destination. After covering quarter of the distance, it starts raining and the train has to be slowed to speed of 75 miles/hour. What is the total journey duration? Choices: A)10 B)11.5 C)12.5 D)13.5 E)15", "step": "Distance to destination = 100 X 10 = 1000 miles.\nDistance remaining when it starts to rain = 1000 - 250 = 750 miles.\nSpeed for remaining distance = 75 miles / hour.\nTime taken to cover remaining distance = 750 / 75 = 10 hours.\nTotal duration of the journey = 2.5 + 10 = 12.5 hours.\nThe correct option is C.", "answer": "C"}, "Answer": "C", "Step": "10% of 250 = 25.\nTotal salary required = 1000\nEarning from single sale = 25\n# of sales = 1000/25 =40\nSo 40 sales\nD is the correct choice", "All_answers": [{"Math Solver3NNA": ["Let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. The train takes 10 hours to reach its destination at a speed of 100 miles/hour. This means the total distance is:\n\nDistance = Speed \u00d7 Time = 100 \u00d7 10 = 1000 miles\n\n2. The train covers a quarter of the distance at 100 miles/hour. This means it covers:\n\nQuarter distance = 1000 \u00d7 1/4 = 250 miles\n\nat a speed of 100 miles/hour. The time taken to cover this quarter distance is:\n\nTime = Distance / Speed = 250 / 100 = 2.5 hours\n\n3. After covering the quarter distance, the train slows down to 75 miles/hour. The remaining distance is:\n\nRemaining distance = 1000 - 250 = 750 miles\n\nThe train takes:\n\nTime = Distance / Speed = 750 / 75 = 10 hours\n\nto cover the remaining distance at a speed of 75 miles/hour.\n\n4. The total journey duration is the sum of the time taken to cover the quarter distance and the time taken to cover the remaining distance:\n\nTotal journey duration = 2.5 + 10 = 12.5 hours\n\nThe answer is C"], "Mathematical AnalystAANW": ["A nice problem to analyze and solve.\n\nLet's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. The train