ular solid is inscribed in the sphere, so that all eight of its vertices are on the sphere. This means that the distance from the center of the sphere to one of the vertices of the solid is equal to the distance from the center of the sphere to the opposite vertex of the solid.\n\nTherefore, we can write:\n\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + (3/2)\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + (15/2)\u00b2\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\n\nNow, we can solve for r:\n\nr\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 112.25\nr\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 112.25\nr\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 112.25\n\nWe can use the fact that the rectangular solid is inscribed in the sphere, so that all eight of its vertices are on the sphere. This means that the distance from the center of the sphere to one of the vertices of the solid is equal to the distance from the center of the sphere to the opposite vertex of the solid.\n\nTherefore, we can write:\n\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + (3/2)\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + (15/2)\u00b2\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\n\nNow, we can solve for r:\n\nr\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 112.25\nr\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 112.25\nr\u00b2 = d\u00b2 - 112.25\n\nWe can use the fact that the rectangular solid is inscribed in the sphere, so that all eight of its vertices are on the sphere. This means that the distance from the center of the sphere to one of the vertices of the solid is equal to the distance from the center of the sphere to the opposite vertex of the solid.\n\nTherefore, we can write:\n\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + (3/2)\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + (15/2)\u00b2\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\nd\u00b2 = r\u00b2 + 112.25\n\nNow, we can"], "Programming ExpertT2nF": ["```python\n\nimport math\n\ndef diameter_of_sphere():\n    # Define the dimensions of the rectangular solid\n    a = 3\n    b = 4\n    c = 15\n    \n    # Calculate the diagonal of the rectangular solid\n    diagonal 